  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CA: Innovation to Impact 2.0</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(USAID Bureau for Resilience and Food Security (RFS)):  Purpose: This activity will conduct research on challenges to widespread adoption of technologies and innovations, and create pathways to enable widespread adoption of improved varieties and other technologies.  $1 million of funding within this IM contributes to meeting the required &quot;Research and Development&quot; directive of $148.8 million and the required &quot;Feed the Future Innovation Labs&quot; sub-directive of $58 million...Activities: Potential activities include: 1) Harmonize tools and approaches to facilitate dissemination and adoption of improved seeds, technologies and practices. This includes harmonizing the use of target product profiles, a stage gate approach to product advancement, and potential use of shared digital tools and platforms that support commercialization processes; 2) Identify and connect actors, including intermediaries and public and private sector partners, that provide essential functions along the dissemination pathway; 3) Identify mechanisms and/or institutional arrangements to create the linkage between innovation and technology transfer pathway; and 4) Design and manage research to identify constraints to achieving widespread technology adoption, best practice approaches to facilitate scale and to evaluate the impact of research investments..Benefitting Countries: TBD.</narrative>
  </description>
